      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The prioritization of political messaging has not diminished the value of contemporary art, as critics and historians increasingly recognize that concept and urgency often outweigh traditional aesthetic standards. By functioning as vital social tools, many works like those of Banksy or Ai WeiWei have achieved critical acclaim by halting cultural change rather than just reflecting it. Ultimately, art's worth is measured by its ability to provoke thought and drive discourse, making political engagement a central pillar of modern artistic value.",
